      "_id": "cTBIOI4EaXmjOmc7",
      "name": "Frost Breath (Recharge 5-6)",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/svg/sword.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>The dragon exhales an icy blast in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a DC 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 36 (8d8) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature who fails their saving throw has their movement speed halved and can't take reactions for 1 minute. If they fail their save by 5 or more, they are also entombed in ice. While entombed, they have total cover and are restrained and incapacitated. At the beginning of their turn, they take 13 (3d8) cold damage and can attempt a DC 18 Strength check, breaking free from the ice on a success. The ice can be attacked and destroyed (AC 10; hp equal to cold damage taken by the breath weapon; vulnerability to fire damage; immunity to cold, poison, and psychic damage).</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
